{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01F3jBTDodpt5izT6TeQS3NZ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# mobile-android: coverage atlas (D1-D24 seen, D25+ forecast)\n2\t\n3\tScope: common Android/mobile CTF concepts mapped against what this lane has shipped and what the harness can handle.\n4\tGround truth (see `reference/techniques/mobile-android.md`): all 23 days shipped the same ~12.7 KB fixture. The day's\n5\tTHEME was flavour only (manifest `huntress.mechanic` + dex `DAY-NN:<theme>:<mechanic>`). The answer `ANS-<16 HEX>` was\n6\tin `assets/huntress_puzzle.json` behind a rotating codec (plain/reverse/base64/xor/split/hex/caesar/native/indexed/\n7\treflection) on D1-D19. D15\n8\tadded the first real extra payload (`lib/x86_64/libarena.so` with the answer as a `.rodata` literal) and mixed-day\n9\tMastery. D16 (JNI Boundary) TT/Mastery builds added the first REAL gate in code: `Java_<pkg>_JNIBoundary_nativeEvidence(int\n10\tlen)` returns `arena_value` only if `len > 0xffff && (u16)len == 0` -- still with the literal in the asset and `.rodata`.\n11\tD17 (Name Collapse, R8-style identifier collapse) left the native track: 6-entry fixture, new per-char permutation codec\n12\t`indexed`, one renamed class `a`; the TT dex carried the real hint `follow b -> a and ignore field c` + `decoy` strings.\n13\tD18 (Encrypted Strings, `string_decryption` \"runtime string decryption\"): 6-entry fixture, codec `xor` again (b64 + 1-byte\n14\tkey); single dex had no cipher code, the TT/Mastery dex added class `EncryptedStrings` method `decryptByte` + `STRUCTURAL`.\n15\tD19 (Reflection Maze, `reflective_dispatch` \"reflective secret dispatch\"; prompt \"Reconstruct reflective dispatch across\n16\tgenerated equivalent call graphs\"): 6-entry fixture, NEW codec name `reflection` whose `data` is the plaintext answer;\n17\tclass `ReflectionMaze`, but NO reflection API in any dex; TT/Mastery dex only added `dispatch` + `STRUCTURAL` strings.\n18\tD20 (Loaded Later, `dynamic_dex` \"secondary DEX loading\"; prompt \"Analyze a challenge-signed secondary DEX and recover\n19\tthe module contract\"): 7-entry APK with `assets/payload.dex` (508 B, plain dex 035); NEW codec `dynamic` whose `data` is\n20\tthe ENTRY PATH `assets/payload.dex` -- the FIRST day the answer left the JSON value: a plain `ANS-` const in payload class\n21\t`com.huntress.arena.payload.Module` (strings `ANSWER`, `CONTRACT`, `DAY20-SIGNED-MODULE:..`). No ClassLoader/verify code\n22\tin any host dex; TT/Mastery host dex added `moduleContract` + `assets/payload.dex:com.huntress.arena.payload.Module`.\n23\tD21 (Debug Me If You Can, `anti_debug` \"anti-debug state checks\"; prompt \"Neutralize a clean-room anti-debug state machine\n24\twhile retaining the intended app flow\"): plain 6-entry fixture, codec back to `reverse` (d2/d8) -- the D20 pointer did\n25\tNOT persist. First manifest with `android:debuggable=\"true\"` (single/TT/Mastery-d21 only). No debugger/TracerPid/clock\n26\tAPI and no state loop in any dex; TT/Mastery dex only added `debuggerGate` + `STRUCTURAL`.\n27\tD22 (Root of Trust, `root_detection` \"synthetic root detection\"; prompt \"Model and bypass multiple synthetic root signals\n28\twithout globally patching success\"): plain 6-entry fixture, codec `base64` (4th time), debuggable false again. No root\n29\tprobe API (File/Build/Runtime.exec/su/magisk) in any dex; TT/Mastery dex only added `rootSignals` + `STRUCTURAL`.\n30\tFIRST 6-set Mastery (d01 plain, d07 caesar, d12 hex, d13 base64, d17 indexed, d22 base64).\n31\tD23 (Hook Line and Signal, `hook_detection` \"hook and instrumentation detection\"; prompt \"Separate real instrumentation\n32\tsignals from generated false positives\"): single = v1 `xor` (key 81). **TT and all 7 Mastery sets (d02, d06, d10, d14,\n33\td15, d22, d23 -- old days REGENERATED) shipped puzzle schema v2 `{\"codec\":\"analysis\",\"build\":..}` with NO data: the answer\n34\tis COMPUTED by dex code** -- `Release.code(Context)` = `\"ANS-\"` + 16 hex nibbles of a static 64-bit mixer chain\n35\t(`token()` = mixA(scanB(mixC(seed))); `scan*` folds in `Probe.s1/s2/s3` 12-bit inverse searches and a theme gate fn such\n36\tas `instrumentationSignals = (a^b^c)&7`; d14 set adds an LCG `long[16]` table walk; d15 set calls JNI `nativeShare(long)`\n37\tin `libarena.so`). Unreferenced look-alike mixers/`K*` consts = the \"generated false positives\". Solved by jadx +\n38\tjavac-with-Context-stub (LLM worker); the solver had no v2 path and `bytecode_vm_scan` resolved 2 of 8 v2 APKs.\n39\tD24 (Emulator Alibi, `emulator_detection` \"emulator environment detection\"; prompt \"Defeat app-owned environment checks on\n40\tthe same pinned emulator used by the solve oracle\"): single = v1 `split` (`parts[3]` + `order [2,0,1]`). TT + FIRST 8-set\n41\tMastery (d03, d06, d09, d10, d15, d17, d23, d24) all v2 `analysis`, same shape as D23: theme = gate fn\n42\t`EmulatorAlibi.emulatorScore(a,b,c) = (a+b+c)%4` over `Probe.s*` ints, decoys `sealEmu*`/`KQemu*`; NO Build/qemu/sensor/\n43\ttelephony API in any dex. The overnight v2 evaluator (lib deep Dalvik eval + solve.py unicorn JNI hop) solved all three\n44\tmodes first try (single 16.3 s via race probe, TT 2.5 s, Mastery 3.1 s).\n45\tSo \"seen Dn\" below means the THEME was named that day; through D22 no exploit was ever needed. D23-D24 TT/Mastery\n46\tcompute the answer in code: assume the timed builds evaluate code, and that tomorrow's theme becomes a gate\n47\tfn / probe set INSIDE the v2 chain (the d10/d14/d22 sets already carry `gateDomain*`/`gateStream*` theme fns).\n48\tD15-D22 read as a MASVS-RESILIENCE / obfuscation arc (native secret -> JNI gate -> name obfuscation + decoys -> string\n49\tencryption -> reflection -> dynamic code loading -> anti-debug -> root detection -> hook (D23) -> emulator (D24)).\n50\tStill unnamed in that arc: tamper/repackaging/installer and attestation (Play Integrity, key attestation -- D22's title pun is\n51\tthe attestation `RootOfTrust` ASN.1 record) checks, then obfuscation capstones (flattening, VM, white-box crypto). After it the untouched MASVS\n52\tgroups are AUTH (biometric/local auth) and the leftover IPC surfaces (bound Service/AIDL, broadcast receivers).\n53\tNext expect also: the payload ENCRYPTED/wrapped (key in host dex, unwrap by\n54\tmagic known plaintext), \"challenge-signed\" made real (several payloads, only the one whose digest/signature matches a\n55\tpinned value is loaded), >1 `ANS-` in the payload with the host-named member (`moduleContract`) deciding, class shadowing\n56\tbetween host and payload loaders, multi-stage loaders, anti-tamper / root / emulator / debugger / Frida checks, and\n57\tcontrol-flow flattening or a tiny VM. New codecs keep arriving (d7 caesar, d15 native, d17 indexed, d19 reflection, d20\n58\tdynamic) and old ones recur (d18 xor, d21 reverse): check `data` for `ANS-`, then for an entry name, then decode from `ANS-` alone.\n59\t\n60\tTool status (after `source bin/env.sh`; checked 2026-10-15). INSTALLED: jadx 1.5.6, apktool 3.0.3, aapt, aapt2,\n61\tapksigner, keytool, jarsigner, d2j-dex2jar (+ `tools/dex2jar/d2j-*.sh`: baksmali, decrypt-string, ...), droidasc,\n62\tandroguard (CLI + py), apkInspector, rizin/rz-bin, r2/rabin2, Ghidra `analyzeHeadless`, readelf/nm/strings, hbc-decompiler/\n63\thbc-disassembler/hbc-file-parser (hermes-dec), ilspycmd + dotnet, webcrack, js-beautify, sqlite3, 7z, binwalk, yara,\n64\ttshark, zlib-flate, openssl, adb (no device). py: lief, pyelftools, capstone, unicorn, pycryptodome, lz4, plistlib.\n65\tMISSING: blutter, reFlutter, pyxamstore, Il2CppDumper/Cpp2IL, frida/frida-tools/objection, apkid, apkleaks, bundletool,\n66\tabe (android-backup-extractor), standalone baksmali/smali, dexdump, zipalign, de4dot, ipsw/plistutil/class-dump.\n67\tTimed constraint: `solve.py` may use only stdlib + lib.* + pyzipper/pyelftools/pefile/capstone/pycryptodome/androguard,\n68\tno subprocess, <1 s per set. Prebuilt extractors must be pure python.\n69\t\n70\t## Concept table\n71\t\n72\tLegend: tool `[i]` = installed here, `[M]` = missing. \"puzzle\" = `assets/huntress_puzzle.json` (`lib.android.puzzle_candidates`).\n73\t\n74\t| # | concept | status | where the answer likely hides | recognition cues | standard tool + exact command | D22+ likelihood |\n75\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n76\t| 1 | Exported Activity / implicit-export default | seen D1 | puzzle; real CTFs: `onCreate` reveals the flag when started with a magic extra | `android:exported=\"true\"`, intent-filter w/o `exported` + targetSdk<31 | `aapt dump xmltree x.apk AndroidManifest.xml` [i]; `droidasc getmanifest x.apk` [i]; `lib.android.manifest_facts` | high: Mastery mixes old days |\n77\t| 2 | Exported Service / AIDL / Messenger | gap | `onBind`/`onStartCommand`/`handleMessage` compares + returns secret | `<service exported>`, `extends Binder`, `$Stub`, `IInterface`, `Messenger` | `jadx -d out x.apk` [i]; `droidasc findrefs x.apk type Landroid/os/Binder;` | med: next IPC theme |\n78\t| 3 | Broadcast receiver (exported, dynamic, ordered/sticky) | gap | `onReceive` action/extra check; action strings in dex | `<receiver exported>`, `registerReceiver`, `sendOrderedBroadcast`, custom `ACTION_*` | `aapt dump xmltree ...`; `jadx` grep `onReceive` | med-high: classic unused IPC theme |\n79\t| 4 | Content provider (SQLi, path traversal, FileProvider paths) | seen D6 | puzzle; real: `query()` / `openFile()`, `res/xml/*paths*.xml` | `<provider exported grantUriPermissions>`, `UriMatcher`, `<root-path>`, `../` | `apktool d -f -o out x.apk` [i]; `aapt dump xmltree x.apk res/xml/file_paths.xml` | med (mixed Mastery) |\n80\t| 5 | Custom permission weakness (normal level, typo, missing) | gap | manifest | `<permission protectionLevel=\"normal\">`, `android:permission` on comp vs `uses-permission` | `aapt dump permissions x.apk` [i] | med |\n81\t| 6 | Task hijacking / StrandHogg | gap | manifest attrs (answer = static) | `taskAffinity`, `allowT