{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013bT9cKmmRZ4DH32MgLbRZF","type":"tool_result","content":"212\t5. Code (after 1-4): jadx -q -d w/j x.apk (--deobf for 1-letter names); droidasc getclass x.apk <cls>\n213\t5a. v2 `analysis` (D23): find what ChallengeActivity appends before `proof=` (Release.code(ctx)); token() = nested static\n214\t   long fns from a const-wide seed; Probe.s1/s2/s3 = <=4096-step inverse searches; theme gate fn (x^y^z)&7 etc.;\n215\t   Tab.build LCG long[16] walk (D14 set). Theme gate = 1 pure fn (D24 emulatorScore=(a+b+c)%4): no device to fake. FAST: copy non-Activity sources, add `package android.content; public class\n216\t   Context {}`, Main prints Release.code(null), javac + java (D23: 7 sets in ~1.5 min). native method -> stub prints its\n217\t   input, compute the export (objdump -d; port to py), feed back. Unreferenced seal*/K* members = decoys. Python port:\n218\t   mask 2^64, `>>>` logical, signed->unsigned before rotate. In solve.py: lib Dalvik evaluator on Release.code only.\n219\t   v1-era hints: R8 \"follow b -> a and ignore field c\" (D17); decryptByte (D18): eval the helper with call-site args.\n220\t6. Native, if no literal: rizin -A -qc 'iE; izz~ANS; afl' f.so ; pdf @ sym.Java_... ; xor loops -> py capstone/unicorn.\n221\t   NEVER ctypes.CDLL / dlopen an artifact .so on the host (sandbox rule) -- emulate or port.\n222\t7. Validate: fullmatch ^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$ (uppercase). v2: also Release.proof == Long.toHexString(token) consistency.\n223\t8. Mastery: each set = different day AND maybe different schema (D23: all v2); decode each APK alone; loop all answer_ids.\n224\t```\n225\t\n226\t## Readiness gaps\n227\t\n228\tPriority 1 = plausible within ~3 days. \"prebuild\" = pure-python extractor in `lib/android.py` style that races in\n229\t`solve.py`. \"tool\" = install. \"note\" = doc/prompt change. Already built or given up (prebuild-state ok / attempts>=2, dropped from the list):\n230\taab-proto-manifest-parse, analysis-android-api-stubs, analysis-chain-obfuscation-hardening,\n231\tanalysis-release-code-eval, ans-prefix-numeric-compose, anti-debug-state-machine-clean-path,\n232\tapk-signing-block-payload, asset-cipher-dex-loader, asset-db-prefs-backup, attestation-jws-claims,\n233\tbinder-ontransact-code-map, biometric-auth-callback-eval, broadcast-receiver-action-map, cdex-vdex-string-pool,\n234\tcert-and-signing-facts, cert-pin-and-nsc-facts, classloader-shadow-resolve, clean-device-env-stubs,\n235\tcustom-alphabet-decode, dalvik-mini-interpreter, dart-snapshot-string-pool, decode-any-chain-peel,\n236\tdecrypt-call-site-args-eval, dex-bytecode-integrity-gate, dex-eval-long-intrinsics, dex-eval-pure-static-memo,\n237\tdex-gated-branch-consts, dex-native-call-args, dex-native-split-assembly, dex-slack-and-header-anomaly,\n238\tdex-string-decrypt-arrays, dispatch-key-resolve, emulator-telephony-sensor-stubs, entry-anchored-candidate-veto,\n239\tentry-reachable-callgraph-rank, enum-switchmap-state-resolve, exception-driven-control-flow,\n240\tflattened-cfg-switch-eval, hermes-hbc-string-table, hook-framework-introspection-stubs, identifier-collision-resolve,\n241\tidentity-derived-key, il2cpp-metadata-literals, installer-source-and-tamper-probe-stubs,\n242\tinstrumentation-false-positive-env, integrity-derived-key, java-serialized-object-parse, jni-export-return-trace,\n243\tjni-gate-bypass-input, jni-reflection-callback, jwt-token-decode-verify, key-attestation-rootoftrust-parse,\n244\tknown-string-obfuscator-signatures, kotlin-metadata-names-and-coroutines, kotlin-object-chain-eval,\n245\tmessagedigest-derived-answer, module-contract-member-eval, multi-abi-arm-native, multi-stage-loader-recurse,\n246\tnative-gated-branch-read, native-init-array-decrypt, native-inline-syscall-stubs, native-libc-probe-stubs-emulate,\n247\tnative-payload-system-load, native-so-emulate-export, native-stack-string, native-system-property-and-mounts-stubs,\n248\tnested-container-recurse, opaque-predicate-dead-branch, payload-digest-pinned-select,\n249\tpayload-magic-known-plaintext-unwrap, permutation-transposition-family, play-integrity-verdict-select,\n250\tprobe-arg-resolve-before-stub, process-exec-shell-probe-stubs, proguard-mapping-restore, proof-flow-candidate-ranking,\n251\tprotobuf-asset-wire-decode, proxy-methodhandle-invokecustom, puzzle-entry-pointer-follow,\n252\tpuzzle-indexed-and-perm-fields, r8-renamed-chain-follow, reflection-name-resolve, registernatives-table,\n253\tresource-id-const-resolve, rolling-xor-keystream-family, root-signal-vector-key, sqlcipher-asset-decrypt,\n254\tstatic-key-cipher-decode, timing-and-debug-flag-probe-stubs, tiny-bytecode-vm-interpret, utf16-string-pool-scan,\n255\tv1-manifest-digest-verify, webview-asset-js-scan, whitebox-table-cipher-eval, xamarin-xalz-blob-unpack,\n256\tzip-structure-anomaly-scan.\n257\tForecast after D24: the MASVS-RESILIENCE arc keeps naming one control per day (D21 anti-debug, D22 root, D23 hook/\n258\tinstrumentation, D24 emulator) and the v2 chain absorbs each one as a single pure gate fn -- D23 and D24 were the same\n259\tgenerator with new names. Still unnamed (D25-D31, 7 days left): anti-tamper / repackaging / APK signature / installer\n260\tsource, self-integrity (dex CRC / checksum), attestation (Play Integrity, key attestation), certificate pinning, then\n261\tobfuscation capstones (flattening, VM, white-box). The next structural step is the chain reading the Context it already\n262\treceives (signature bytes, zip CRC, Build/props, keystore certs) or doing float/Random math; the D24 prompt's \"pinned\n263\temulator used by the solve oracle\" means any environment read must be answered as the oracle's stock AVD, not only as a\n264\tclean Pixel. Mastery grows +1 set per day (D24: 8) -- keep the per-set solve far under the window.\n265\t\n266\t```json[\n267\t  {\"id\": \"worker-cue-inline\", \"concept\": \"unseen-theme routing\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Inline the 'Recognition cues' block above into the mobile worker prompt (skills/huntress-ctf mobile skill) so an unseen container (Flutter/RN/Xamarin/asset dex) is routed in 1-2 turns; add step 2's UTF-16 scan to triage.md pre-extraction.\"},\n268\t  {\"id\": \"pinned-emulator-env-profile\", \"concept\": \"environment probes answered as the solve oracle's PINNED stock emulator, alongside the clean-Pixel profile (rows 48, 99)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D24 prompt: 'Defeat app-owned environment checks on the same pinned emulator used by the solve oracle' -- the reference answer is produced ON an emulator, so if a chain ever reads the environment, the clean-Pixel stubs (clean-device-env-stubs, emulator-telephony-sensor-stubs, analysis-android-api-stubs) may give the WRONG value. Add a second env profile to the deep evaluator and to clean_device_scan: a stock Google AVD x86_64 (Build.FINGERPRINT google/sdk_gphone64_x86_64/emu64x:14/...:userdebug/dev-keys, MODEL sdk_gphone64_x86_64, MANUFACTURER Google, BRAND google, HARDWARE ranchu, PRODUCT sdk_gphone64_x86_64, DEVICE emu64x, BOARD goldfish_x86_64, TAGS dev-keys, TYPE userdebug; ro.kernel.qemu=1, ro.boot.qemu=1, ro.hardware=ranchu, qemu.sf.lcd_density, /dev/qemu_pipe + /dev/goldfish_pipe present; TelephonyManager operator 'Android'/'310260', line1 15555215554, deviceId 358240051111110; sensor list with 'Goldfish 3-axis Accelerometer'; battery 50%/AC). Evaluate the entry under BOTH profiles; if the values differ, return both with labels (emulator first when the prompt says 'pinned emulator'/'solve oracle', clean first otherwise) and log which probe diverged. Keep the clean profile the default for v1 code-side scans.\"},\n269\t  {\"id\": \"analysis-self-integrity-stubs\", \"concept\": \"anti-tamper / repackaging inside the v2 chain: signature bytes, signing-cert digest, own dex CRC / checksum folded into the seed (rows 99, 49)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Likeliest next resilience control (D25+). The chain would do: ctx.getPackageManager().getPackageInfo(pkg, GET_SIGNATURES|GET_SIGNING_CERTIFICATES).signatures[0] -> .hashCode() (= Arrays.hashCode(toByteArray()) Java int semantics) / .toByteArray() -> MessageDigest SHA-256|SHA-1|MD5 -> fold into a long (ByteBuffer.wrap(d).getLong(), or loop `v = v*31 + b`); ctx.getApplicationInfo().sourceDir / getPackageCodePath() -> new ZipFile(path).getEntry(\\\"classes.dex\\\").getCrc() / .getSize(); CRC32/Adler32 over the dex or the puzzle asset; getInstallerPackageName / getInstallSourceInfo -> 'com.android.vending'. Answer every stub from the APK's OWN bytes: signing cert = the PKCS#7 in META-INF/*.RSA|*.DSA|*.EC (v1) or the v2/v3 signing block (signing_certs exists), zip entry CRC/size from the central directory, dex bytes as shipped. Exact Java semantics for Signature.hashCode, String.hashCode, Arrays.hashCode(byte[]), byte sign extension. Test: a synthetic chain over the D24 TT fixture; regression: D23/D24 v2 APKs unchanged.\"},\n270\t  {\"id\": \"dex-eval-float-double-semantics\", \"concept\": \"float/double arithmetic in a v2 chain (sensor readings, scores, thresholds) with exact Java semantics (row 96)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D24 class names already say `SensorMap`/`mixSensor*`; a sensor- or score-based gate would use floats (accelerometer m/s^2, battery temperature, `score > 0.5f`). Make the deep evaluator exact for: add/sub/mul/div/rem-float|double (+2addr), neg-*, int/long<->float/double conversions incl. float-to-int / double-to-long SATURATION and NaN->0, cmpl/cmpg-float|double NaN bias, const/high16 + const-wide/high16 float/double bit patterns, Float.floatToIntBits/floatToRawIntBits/intBitsToFloat, Double.doubleToLongBits/doubleToRawLongBits/longBitsToDouble, Math.round/floor/ceil/sqrt/abs/pow/min/max, StrictMath, Float.compare. Use struct pack/unpack('<f') for float32 rounding after every float op. Unit-test each opcode against known Java outputs.\"},\n271\t  {\"id\": \"dex-eval-native-bridge\", \"concept\": \"Dalvik evaluator calls a `native` method mid-chain by emulating its `Java_*` export (rows 37, 96)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D23 Mastery d15 set: `NativeLibrarySecrets.nativeShare(long)` (static native, `System.loadLibrary(\\\"arena\\\")` in <clinit>) sits inside Release.token(); `lib/x86_64/libarena.so` (13512 B) exports `Java_<pkg>_NativeLibrarySecrets_nativeShare` = ~10 insns of movabs/add/xor/imul/rol on rdx. The LLM worker used ctypes.CDLL on the host (sandbox violation). In the evaluator: when invoke-static/virtual hits a method with ACC_NATIVE, mangle the JNI name (incl. overloaded `__<sig>` form and `_1`/`_0xxxx` escapes), find the export in lib/<abi>/*.so (x86_64 first, then arm64-v8a/armeabi-v7a/x86), and run it under unicorn (reuse native-so-emulate-export): JNIEnv* -> a fake function table whose slots return 0/trap, jclass/jobject = dummy handles, long/int args per SysV (rdx, rcx, r8...) or AAPCS64 (x2, x3...), return rax/x0 masked to the declared type; jstring returns via a NewStringUTF stub that records the C string. Budget 200k insns. Also support RegisterNatives tables (registernatives-table built). Never dlopen the artifact.\"},\n272\t  {\"id\": \"dex-eval-java-random-lcg\", \"concept\": \"java.util.Random / SplittableRandom / ThreadLocalRandom-free determinism inside the v2 evaluator (row 96)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"lib already carries the 0x5DEECE66D LCG for v1 scans; the deep evaluator (`_DxeDeepVM`) needs it as intrinsics: new Random(long) (seed ^ 0x5DEECE66D, 48-bit), nextInt(), nextInt(bound) incl. the power-of-two and rejection loop, nextLong(), nextBoolean(), nextDouble() (26+27 bits), nextBytes(byte[]), setSeed; java.util.SplittableRandom(seed).nextLong()/nextInt (mix64 / GOLDEN_GAMMA); Collections.shuffle(list, rnd); UUID.nameUUIDFromBytes (MD5). Unseeded new Random()/Math.random()/System.nanoTime -> report 'non-deterministic' and abort that candidate rather than invent a value.\"},\n273\t  {\"id\": \"analysis-keystore-cert-api-stubs\", \"concept\": \"attestation / keystore theme inside the v2 chain: certificate chain bytes and the attestation extension read through KeyStore / CertificateFactory APIs (rows 87, 93)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Attestation is still unnamed in the arc. A v2 version would read a shipped cert: ctx.getResources().openRawResource(R.raw.x) or getAssets().open('attest.der'|'.pem') -> CertificateFactory.getInstance(\\\"X.509\\\").generateCertificate(in) / generateCertificates -> X509Certificate.getExtensionValue(\\\"1.3.6.1.4.1.11129.2.1.17\\\") (OCTET STRING-wrapped DER), getEncoded(), getPublicKey().getEncoded(), getSerialNumber().longValue(), getNotBefore().getTime(), getSubjectX500Principal().getName(); KeyStore.getInstance(\\\"AndroidKeyStore\\\").getCertificateChain(alias) -> the shipped chain in order. Implement as evaluator objects backed by the APK's own cert bytes (asn1 via the existing key-attestation-rootoftrust-parse helpers): byte[] results as Python bytearrays with Java signed-byte reads, BigInteger.longValue truncation.\"},\n274\t  {\"id\": \"analysis-interface-signal-list-eval\", \"concept\": \"signals as objects: interface/abstract `Signal` implementations collected in ArrayList/HashMap and iterated, virtual dispatch in the v2 evaluator (rows 94, 96)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D22-D24 'multiple signals' prompts have so far meant three static Probe calls; the natural next generator step is `List<Check> checks = Arrays.asList(new BoardCheck(), new SensorMap(), ...); for (Check c : checks) score += c.weight() * c.read();`. Support in the deep evaluator: new-instance + <init> + iget/iput (incl. -wide/-object/-boolean), invoke-virtual/-interface dispatch by runtime class (walk superclass chain, default interface methods), java.util.ArrayList/Arrays.asList/List.of/Iterator/for-each, HashMap/LinkedHashMap put/get/entrySet iteration order (insertion for Linked, Java hash order for HashMap -- implement String.hashCode bucket order for small maps), StringBuilder.reverse/insert/setCharAt, String.format('%02x'), Integer.valueOf caching/unboxing. Budget unchanged (<0.3 s per set).\"},\n275\t  {\"id\": \"native-bridge-jnienv-callbacks\", \"concept\": \"JNI export inside the v2 chain that calls back into JNIEnv (strings, static fields, Java methods) (rows 37, 82, 96)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D23/D24 d15 set `nativeShare(long)` is pure arithmetic; the next native step uses the env: GetStringUTFChars/ReleaseStringUTFChars on a jstring arg, NewStringUTF result, GetArrayLength/GetByteArrayElements/GetByteArrayRegion on a byte[] arg, FindClass + GetStaticFieldID + GetStaticLongField/GetStaticIntField (read a dex `K*` const), GetStaticMethodID + CallStaticLongMethod(A|V) back into a dex mixer. In solve.py-style unicorn harness (`_native_call`): build a real JNINativeInterface function table (229 slots, each a hook address), resolve each called slot by index, service it from the Dalvik evaluator (strings via a handle table, callbacks re-entering `_DxeDeepVM.run`), then resume. Support x86_64 and arm64-v8a. Never dlopen the artifact.\"},\n276\t  {\"id\": \"analysis-cert-pin-digest-chain\", \"concept\": \"certificate-pinning theme in the v2 chain: SPKI SHA-256 pins computed from a shipped cert and compared / folded (rows 27, 28, 96)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Pinning (D9 trust manager, D10 NSC) has only been flavour; a resilience-arc 'pinning bypass' day would compute `sha256/` + base64(SHA-256(SubjectPublicKeyInfo DER)) of res/raw|assets cert(s) and compare to the NSC `<pin digest=\\\"SHA-256\\\">` / OkHttp CertificatePinner string, folding the match index or the digest bytes into the seed. Provide: SPKI extraction from X.509 DER (asn1 walk, no openssl subprocess), Base64.encodeToString flags (NO_WRAP/DEFAULT newline), MessageDigest intrinsics, NSC pin-set parse from res/xml (binary XML via aapt-free lib parser), and expiry-date compare. Report which pin matched which cert.\"},\n277\t  {\"id\": \"mastery-set-scaling-bench\", \"concept\": \"Mastery grows +1 set per day (5,6,7,8): keep every v2 set solvable inside the window as the bundle grows (row 96)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D24 8 sets solved in 0.94 s (TT single set 0.39 s), with one forked process per set. At +1/day D31 could carry ~15 sets including several JNI/unicorn sets. Build a bench (tests or tools script, pure python) that runs the deep evaluator over every v2 fixture under challenges/day2[34]/**/cases and fails if any set > 0.4 s or the total of a 15-set synthetic bundle (fixtures repeated) > 3 s on one core; profile and fix hotspots (unicorn Uc construction per call -> cache per .so; dex parse per set -> cache by sha256; Probe inverse searches -> closed form when f is affine mod 4096).\"},\n278\t  {\"id\": \"generalize-before-stop\", \"concept\": \"carry the hand-solved method into solve.py when a live worker reaches CORRECT first\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D23: hand-solved TT/Mastery left solve.py without a v2 path; the overnight prebuild fixed it and D24 went 3/3 on the solver alone. Keep the rule: when a timed mode is CORRECT via a live worker, let one generalize worker finish offline and require `hctf solver-test` on the variant-* cases with expected.json filled from confirmed.json.\"},\n279\t  {\"id\": \"pyxamstore\", \"concept\": \"Xamarin assemblies.blob / XALZ (row 55)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python pyxamstore` (or github jakev/pyxamstore). Then `pyxamstore unpack -d assemblies/` and ilspycmd. Also small prebuild: XALZ header (magic, index, size) + lz4.block decompress (lz4 in venv).\"},\n280\t  {\"id\": \"apkid\", \"concept\": \"packer / obfuscator / anti-VM identification (rows 44-48)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python apkid` (needs yara-python, already OK). `apkid -j x.apk` names packers, obfuscators and anti-debug in one call: a fast routing cue for an unseen theme.\"},\n281\t  {\"id\": \"bundletool\", \"concept\": \"AAB / APKS packaging (row 58)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release jar google/bundletool (bundletool-all-1.17.x.jar) into tools/bundletool + bin shim. `bundletool dump manifest --bundle x.aab`, `bundletool build-apks --mode=universal`. AAB manifests are protobuf, so aapt dump xmltree fails on them.\"},\n282\t  {\"id\": \"ios-ipa-readiness\", \"concept\": \"iOS IPA (row 64)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Lane is named mobile-android; if an .ipa ever ships: unzip Payload/, plistlib for Info.plist and binary plists, rz-bin -zz / lief for Mach-O strings, ipsw (github blacktop/ipsw release) for class-dump. Nothing to prebuild now.\"},\n283\t  {\"id\": \"il2cppdumper\", \"concept\": \"Unity IL2CPP (row 56)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release Perfare/Il2CppDumper (or SamboyCoding/Cpp2IL) into tools/; run with bin/dotnet. Only if a Unity fixture ever ships.\"},\n284\t  {\"id\": \"blutter\", \"concept\": \"Flutter Dart AOT (row 52)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github worawit/blutter (python3 blutter.py <lib dir> <out>; builds per Dart version with cmake/ninja + fetches the Dart SDK, slow first run; arm64 only). Alt: pip reflutter (needs repack + device: low value). Plain strings on libapp.so cover literal answers.\"},\n285\t  {\"id\": \"abe\", \"concept\": \"encrypted Android backup (row 16)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release nelenkov/android-backup-extractor (abe.jar): `java -jar abe.jar unpack b.ab b.tar [pw]`. Needed only for encrypted .ab (PBKDF2+AES); unencrypted is zlib-flate.\"},\n286\t  {\"id\": \"frida-tools\", \"concept\": \"dynamic instrumentation / root and frida checks (rows 47, 48)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip frida-tools / objection. Low value: no Android device or emulator here (adb present, no target), and every answer so far was static. Keep the rule: read the gated branch statically.\"},\n287\t  {\"id\": \"standalone-baksmali\", \"concept\": \"smali-level reading / patching (row 51)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"Link tools/dex2jar/d2j-baksmali.sh + d2j-smali.sh into bin/ (already on disk), or github google/smali release. apktool d already emits smali, so cosmetic.\"}\n288\t]\n289\t```\n290\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"42f33c12-3125-441c-8886-1e987da4999d","uuid":"2bbdd86d-1add-4b78-b422-fa5c84e2db76","timestamp":"2026-10-25T13:07:00.575Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/coverage/mobile-android.md","content":"5. Code (after 1-4): jadx -q -d w/j x.apk (--deobf for 1-letter names); droidasc getclass x.apk <cls>\n5a. v2 `analysis` (D23): find what ChallengeActivity appends before `proof=` (Release.code(ctx)); token() = nested static\n   long fns from a const-wide seed; Probe.s1/s2/s3 = <=4096-step inverse searches; theme gate fn (x^y^z)&7 etc.;\n   Tab.build LCG long[16] walk (D14 set). Theme gate = 1 pure fn (D24 emulatorScore=(a+b+c)%4): no device to fake. FAST: copy non-Activity sources, add `package android.content; public class\n   Context {}`, Main prints Release.code(null), javac + java (D23: 7 sets in ~1.5 min). native method -> stub prints its\n   input, compute the export (objdump -d; port to py), feed back. Unreferenced seal*/K* members = decoys. Python port:\n   mask 2^64, `>>>` logical, signed->unsigned before rotate. In solve.py: lib Dalvik evaluator on Release.code only.\n   v1-era hints: R8 \"follow b -> a and ignore field c\" (D17); decryptByte (D18): eval the helper with call-site args.\n6. Native, if no literal: rizin -A -qc 'iE; izz~ANS; afl' f.so ; pdf @ sym.Java_... ; xor loops -> py capstone/unicorn.\n   NEVER ctypes.CDLL / dlopen an artifact .so on the host (sandbox rule) -- emulate or port.\n7. Validate: fullmatch ^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$ (uppercase). v2: also Release.proof == Long.toHexString(token) consistency.\n8. Mastery: each set = different day AND maybe different schema (D23: all v2); decode each APK alone; loop all answer_ids.\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\n\nPriority 1 = plausible within ~3 days. \"prebuild\" = pure-python extractor in `lib/android.py` style that races in\n`solve.py`. \"tool\" = install. \"note\" = doc/prompt change. Already built or given up (prebuild-state ok / attempts>=2, dropped from the list):\naab-proto-manifest-parse, analysis-android-api-stubs, analysis-chain-obfuscation-hardening,\nanalysis-release-code-eval, ans-prefix-numeric-compose, anti-debug-state-machine-clean-path,\napk-signing-block-payload, asset-cipher-dex-loader, asset-db-prefs-backup, attestation-jws-claims,\nbinder-ontransact-code-map, biometric-auth-callback-eval, broadcast-receiver-action-map, cdex-vdex-string-pool,\ncert-and-signing-facts, cert-pin-and-nsc-facts, classloader-shadow-resolve, clean-device-env-stubs,\ncustom-alphabet-decode, dalvik-mini-interpreter, dart-snapshot-string-pool, decode-any-chain-peel,\ndecrypt-call-site-args-eval, dex-bytecode-integrity-gate, dex-eval-long-intrinsics, dex-eval-pure-static-memo,\ndex-gated-branch-consts, dex-native-call-args, dex-native-split-assembly, dex-slack-and-header-anomaly,\ndex-string-decrypt-arrays, dispatch-key-resolve, emulator-telephony-sensor-stubs, entry-anchored-candidate-veto,\nentry-reachable-callgraph-rank, enum-switchmap-state-resolve, exception-driven-control-flow,\nflattened-cfg-switch-eval, hermes-hbc-string-table, hook-framework-introspection-stubs, identifier-collision-resolve,\nidentity-derived-key, il2cpp-metadata-literals, installer-source-and-tamper-probe-stubs,\ninstrumentation-false-positive-env, integrity-derived-key, java-serialized-object-parse, jni-export-return-trace,\njni-gate-bypass-input, jni-reflection-callback, jwt-token-decode-verify, key-attestation-rootoftrust-parse,\nknown-string-obfuscator-signatures, kotlin-metadata-names-and-coroutines, kotlin-object-chain-eval,\nmessagedigest-derived-answer, module-contract-member-eval, multi-abi-arm-native, multi-stage-loader-recurse,\nnative-gated-branch-read, native-init-array-decrypt, native-inline-syscall-stubs, native-libc-probe-stubs-emulate,\nnative-payload-system-load, native-so-emulate-export, native-stack-string, native-system-property-and-mounts-stubs,\nnested-container-recurse, opaque-predicate-dead-branch, payload-digest-pinned-select,\npayload-magic-known-plaintext-unwrap, permutation-transposition-family, play-integrity-verdict-select,\nprobe-arg-resolve-before-stub, process-exec-shell-probe-stubs, proguard-mapping-restore, proof-flow-candidate-ranking,\nprotobuf-asset-wire-decode, proxy-methodhandle-invokecustom, puzzle-entry-pointer-follow,\npuzzle-indexed-and-perm-fields, r8-renamed-chain-follow, reflection-name-resolve, registernatives-table,\nresource-id-const-resolve, rolling-xor-keystream-family, root-signal-vector-key, sqlcipher-asset-decrypt,\nstatic-key-cipher-decode, timing-and-debug-flag-probe-stubs, tiny-bytecode-vm-interpret, utf16-string-pool-scan,\nv1-manifest-digest-verify, webview-asset-js-scan, whitebox-table-cipher-eval, xamarin-xalz-blob-unpack,\nzip-structure-anomaly-scan.\nForecast after D24: the MASVS-RESILIENCE arc keeps naming one control per day (D21 anti-debug, D22 root, D23 hook/\ninstrumentation, D24 emulator) and the v2 chain absorbs each one as a single pure gate fn -- D23 and D24 were the same\ngenerator with new names. Still unnamed (D25-D31, 7 days left): anti-tamper / repackaging / APK signature / installer\nsource, self-integrity (dex CRC / checksum), attestation (Play Integrity, key attestation), certificate pinning, then\nobfuscation capstones (flattening, VM, white-box). The next structural step is the chain reading the Context it already\nreceives (signature bytes, zip CRC, Build/props, keystore certs) or doing float/Random math; the D24 prompt's \"pinned\nemulator used by the solve oracle\" means any environment read must be answered as the oracle's stock AVD, not only as a\nclean Pixel. Mastery grows +1 set per day (D24: 8) -- keep the per-set solve far under the window.\n\n```json[\n  {\"id\": \"worker-cue-inline\", \"concept\": \"unseen-theme routing\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Inline the 'Recognition cues' block above into the mobile worker prompt (skills/huntress-ctf mobile skill) so an unseen container (Flutter/RN/Xamarin/asset dex) is routed in 1-2 turns; add step 2's UTF-16 scan to triage.md pre-extraction.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"pinned-emulator-env-profile\", \"concept\": \"environment probes answered as the solve oracle's PINNED stock emulator, alongside the clean-Pixel profile (rows 48, 99)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D24 prompt: 'Defeat app-owned environment checks on the same pinned emulator used by the solve oracle' -- the reference answer is produced ON an emulator, so if a chain ever reads the environment, the clean-Pixel stubs (clean-device-env-stubs, emulator-telephony-sensor-stubs, analysis-android-api-stubs) may give the WRONG value. Add a second env profile to the deep evaluator and to clean_device_scan: a stock Google AVD x86_64 (Build.FINGERPRINT google/sdk_gphone64_x86_64/emu64x:14/...:userdebug/dev-keys, MODEL sdk_gphone64_x86_64, MANUFACTURER Google, BRAND google, HARDWARE ranchu, PRODUCT sdk_gphone64_x86_64, DEVICE emu64x, BOARD goldfish_x86_64, TAGS dev-keys, TYPE userdebug; ro.kernel.qemu=1, ro.boot.qemu=1, ro.hardware=ranchu, qemu.sf.lcd_density, /dev/qemu_pipe + /dev/goldfish_pipe present; TelephonyManager operator 'Android'/'310260', line1 15555215554, deviceId 358240051111110; sensor list with 'Goldfish 3-axis Accelerometer'; battery 50%/AC). Evaluate the entry under BOTH profiles; if the values differ, return both with labels (emulator first when the prompt says 'pinned emulator'/'solve oracle', clean first otherwise) and log which probe diverged. Keep the clean profile the default for v1 code-side scans.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"analysis-self-integrity-stubs\", \"concept\": \"anti-tamper / repackaging inside the v2 chain: signature bytes, signing-cert digest, own dex CRC / checksum folded into the seed (rows 99, 49)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Likeliest next resilience control (D25+). The chain would do: ctx.getPackageManager().getPackageInfo(pkg, GET_SIGNATURES|GET_SIGNING_CERTIFICATES).signatures[0] -> .hashCode() (= Arrays.hashCode(toByteArray()) Java int semantics) / .toByteArray() -> MessageDigest SHA-256|SHA-1|MD5 -> fold into a long (ByteBuffer.wrap(d).getLong(), or loop `v = v*31 + b`); ctx.getApplicationInfo().sourceDir / getPackageCodePath() -> new ZipFile(path).getEntry(\\\"classes.dex\\\").getCrc() / .getSize(); CRC32/Adler32 over the dex or the puzzle asset; getInstallerPackageName / getInstallSourceInfo -> 'com.android.vending'. Answer every stub from the APK's OWN bytes: signing cert = the PKCS#7 in META-INF/*.RSA|*.DSA|*.EC (v1) or the v2/v3 signing block (signing_certs exists), zip entry CRC/size from the central directory, dex bytes as shipped. Exact Java semantics for Signature.hashCode, String.hashCode, Arrays.hashCode(byte[]), byte sign extension. Test: a synthetic chain over the D24 TT fixture; regression: D23/D24 v2 APKs unchanged.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dex-eval-float-double-semantics\", \"concept\": \"float/double arithmetic in a v2 chain (sensor readings, scores, thresholds) with exact Java semantics (row 96)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D24 class names already say `SensorMap`/`mixSensor*`; a sensor- or score-based gate would use floats (accelerometer m/s^2, battery temperature, `score > 0.5f`). Make the deep evaluator exact for: add/sub/mul/div/rem-float|double (+2addr), neg-*, int/long<->float/double conversions incl. float-to-int / double-to-long SATURATION and NaN->0, cmpl/cmpg-float|double NaN bias, const/high16 + const-wide/high16 float/double bit patterns, Float.floatToIntBits/floatToRawIntBits/intBitsToFloat, Double.doubleToLongBits/doubleToRawLongBits/longBitsToDouble, Math.round/floor/ceil/sqrt/abs/pow/min/max, StrictMath, Float.compare. Use struct pack/unpack('<f') for float32 rounding after every float op. Unit-test each opcode against known Java outputs.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dex-eval-native-bridge\", \"concept\": \"Dalvik evaluator calls a `native` method mid-chain by emulating its `Java_*` export (rows 37, 96)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D23 Mastery d15 set: `NativeLibrarySecrets.nativeShare(long)` (static native, `System.loadLibrary(\\\"arena\\\")` in <clinit>) sits inside Release.token(); `lib/x86_64/libarena.so` (13512 B) exports `Java_<pkg>_NativeLibrarySecrets_nativeShare` = ~10 insns of movabs/add/xor/imul/rol on rdx. The LLM worker used ctypes.CDLL on the host (sandbox violation). In the evaluator: when invoke-static/virtual hits a method with ACC_NATIVE, mangle the JNI name (incl. overloaded `__<sig>` form and `_1`/`_0xxxx` escapes), find the export in lib/<abi>/*.so (x86_64 first, then arm64-v8a/armeabi-v7a/x86), and run it under unicorn (reuse native-so-emulate-export): JNIEnv* -> a fake function table whose slots return 0/trap, jclass/jobject = dummy handles, long/int args per SysV (rdx, rcx, r8...) or AAPCS64 (x2, x3...), return rax/x0 masked to the declared type; jstring returns via a NewStringUTF stub that records the C string. Budget 200k insns. Also support RegisterNatives tables (registernatives-table built). Never dlopen the artifact.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dex-eval-java-random-lcg\", \"concept\": \"java.util.Random / SplittableRandom / ThreadLocalRandom-free determinism inside the v2 evaluator (row 96)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"lib already carries the 0x5DEECE66D LCG for v1 scans; the deep evaluator (`_DxeDeepVM`) needs it as intrinsics: new Random(long) (seed ^ 0x5DEECE66D, 48-bit), nextInt(), nextInt(bound) incl. the power-of-two and rejection loop, nextLong(), nextBoolean(), nextDouble() (26+27 bits), nextBytes(byte[]), setSeed; java.util.SplittableRandom(seed).nextLong()/nextInt (mix64 / GOLDEN_GAMMA); Collections.shuffle(list, rnd); UUID.nameUUIDFromBytes (MD5). Unseeded new Random()/Math.random()/System.nanoTime -> report 'non-deterministic' and abort that candidate rather than invent a value.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"analysis-keystore-cert-api-stubs\", \"concept\": \"attestation / keystore theme inside the v2 chain: certificate chain bytes and the attestation extension read through KeyStore / CertificateFactory APIs (rows 87, 93)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Attestation is still unnamed in the arc. A v2 version would read a shipped cert: ctx.getResources().openRawResource(R.raw.x) or getAssets().open('attest.der'|'.pem') -> CertificateFactory.getInstance(\\\"X.509\\\").generateCertificate(in) / generateCertificates -> X509Certificate.getExtensionValue(\\\"1.3.6.1.4.1.11129.2.1.17\\\") (OCTET STRING-wrapped DER), getEncoded(), getPublicKey().getEncoded(), getSerialNumber().longValue(), getNotBefore().getTime(), getSubjectX500Principal().getName(); KeyStore.getInstance(\\\"AndroidKeyStore\\\").getCertificateChain(alias) -> the shipped chain in order. Implement as evaluator objects backed by the APK's own cert bytes (asn1 via the existing key-attestation-rootoftrust-parse helpers): byte[] results as Python bytearrays with Java signed-byte reads, BigInteger.longValue truncation.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"analysis-interface-signal-list-eval\", \"concept\": \"signals as objects: interface/abstract `Signal` implementations collected in ArrayList/HashMap and iterated, virtual dispatch in the v2 evaluator (rows 94, 96)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D22-D24 'multiple signals' prompts have so far meant three static Probe calls; the natural next generator step is `List<Check> checks = Arrays.asList(new BoardCheck(), new SensorMap(), ...); for (Check c : checks) score += c.weight() * c.read();`. Support in the deep evaluator: new-instance + <init> + iget/iput (incl. -wide/-object/-boolean), invoke-virtual/-interface dispatch by runtime class (walk superclass chain, default interface methods), java.util.ArrayList/Arrays.asList/List.of/Iterator/for-each, HashMap/LinkedHashMap put/get/entrySet iteration order (insertion for Linked, Java hash order for HashMap -- implement String.hashCode bucket order for small maps), StringBuilder.reverse/insert/setCharAt, String.format('%02x'), Integer.valueOf caching/unboxing. Budget unchanged (<0.3 s per set).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"native-bridge-jnienv-callbacks\", \"concept\": \"JNI export inside the v2 chain that calls back into JNIEnv (strings, static fields, Java methods) (rows 37, 82, 96)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D23/D24 d15 set `nativeShare(long)` is pure arithmetic; the next native step uses the env: GetStringUTFChars/ReleaseStringUTFChars on a jstring arg, NewStringUTF result, GetArrayLength/GetByteArrayElements/GetByteArrayRegion on a byte[] arg, FindClass + GetStaticFieldID + GetStaticLongField/GetStaticIntField (read a dex `K*` const), GetStaticMethodID + CallStaticLongMethod(A|V) back into a dex mixer. In solve.py-style unicorn harness (`_native_call`): build a real JNINativeInterface function table (229 slots, each a hook address), resolve each called slot by index, service it from the Dalvik evaluator (strings via a handle table, callbacks re-entering `_DxeDeepVM.run`), then resume. Support x86_64 and arm64-v8a. Never dlopen the artifact.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"analysis-cert-pin-digest-chain\", \"concept\": \"certificate-pinning theme in the v2 chain: SPKI SHA-256 pins computed from a shipped cert and compared / folded (rows 27, 28, 96)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Pinning (D9 trust manager, D10 NSC) has only been flavour; a resilience-arc 'pinning bypass' day would compute `sha256/` + base64(SHA-256(SubjectPublicKeyInfo DER)) of res/raw|assets cert(s) and compare to the NSC `<pin digest=\\\"SHA-256\\\">` / OkHttp CertificatePinner string, folding the match index or the digest bytes into the seed. Provide: SPKI extraction from X.509 DER (asn1 walk, no openssl subprocess), Base64.encodeToString flags (NO_WRAP/DEFAULT newline), MessageDigest intrinsics, NSC pin-set parse from res/xml (binary XML via aapt-free lib parser), and expiry-date compare. Report which pin matched which cert.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"mastery-set-scaling-bench\", \"concept\": \"Mastery grows +1 set per day (5,6,7,8): keep every v2 set solvable inside the window as the bundle grows (row 96)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D24 8 sets solved in 0.94 s (TT single set 0.39 s), with one forked process per set. At +1/day D31 could carry ~15 sets including several JNI/unicorn sets. Build a bench (tests or tools script, pure python) that runs the deep evaluator over every v2 fixture under challenges/day2[34]/**/cases and fails if any set > 0.4 s or the total of a 15-set synthetic bundle (fixtures repeated) > 3 s on one core; profile and fix hotspots (unicorn Uc construction per call -> cache per .so; dex parse per set -> cache by sha256; Probe inverse searches -> closed form when f is affine mod 4096).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"generalize-before-stop\", \"concept\": \"carry the hand-solved method into solve.py when a live worker reaches CORRECT first\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D23: hand-solved TT/Mastery left solve.py without a v2 path; the overnight prebuild fixed it and D24 went 3/3 on the solver alone. Keep the rule: when a timed mode is CORRECT via a live worker, let one generalize worker finish offline and require `hctf solver-test` on the variant-* cases with expected.json filled from confirmed.json.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"pyxamstore\", \"concept\": \"Xamarin assemblies.blob / XALZ (row 55)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python pyxamstore` (or github jakev/pyxamstore). Then `pyxamstore unpack -d assemblies/` and ilspycmd. Also small prebuild: XALZ header (magic, index, size) + lz4.block decompress (lz4 in venv).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"apkid\", \"concept\": \"packer / obfuscator / anti-VM identification (rows 44-48)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python apkid` (needs yara-python, already OK). `apkid -j x.apk` names packers, obfuscators and anti-debug in one call: a fast routing cue for an unseen theme.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"bundletool\", \"concept\": \"AAB / APKS packaging (row 58)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release jar google/bundletool (bundletool-all-1.17.x.jar) into tools/bundletool + bin shim. `bundletool dump manifest --bundle x.aab`, `bundletool build-apks --mode=universal`. AAB manifests are protobuf, so aapt dump xmltree fails on them.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ios-ipa-readiness\", \"concept\": \"iOS IPA (row 64)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Lane is named mobile-android; if an .ipa ever ships: unzip Payload/, plistlib for Info.plist and binary plists, rz-bin -zz / lief for Mach-O strings, ipsw (github blacktop/ipsw release) for class-dump. Nothing to prebuild now.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"il2cppdumper\", \"concept\": \"Unity IL2CPP (row 56)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release Perfare/Il2CppDumper (or SamboyCoding/Cpp2IL) into tools/; run with bin/dotnet. Only if a Unity fixture ever ships.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"blutter\", \"concept\": \"Flutter Dart AOT (row 52)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github worawit/blutter (python3 blutter.py <lib dir> <out>; builds per Dart version with cmake/ninja + fetches the Dart SDK, slow first run; arm64 only). Alt: pip reflutter (needs repack + device: low value). Plain strings on libapp.so cover literal answers.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"abe\", \"concept\": \"encrypted Android backup (row 16)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release nelenkov/android-backup-extractor (abe.jar): `java -jar abe.jar unpack b.ab b.tar [pw]`. Needed only for encrypted .ab (PBKDF2+AES); unencrypted is zlib-flate.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"frida-tools\", \"concept\": \"dynamic instrumentation / root and frida checks (rows 47, 48)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip frida-tools / objection. Low value: no Android device or emulator here (adb present, no target), and every answer so far was static. Keep the rule: read the gated branch statically.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"standalone-baksmali\", \"concept\": \"smali-level reading / patching (row 51)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"Link tools/dex2jar/d2j-baksmali.sh + d2j-smali.sh into bin/ (already on disk), or github google/smali release. apktool d already emits smali, so cosmetic.\"}\n]\n```\n","numLines":79,"startLine":212,"totalLines":290}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013bT9cKmmRZ4DH32MgLbRZF","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
