{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgP1io5zPkGkEBXEt9ABg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Np14p3whLXDSKEbDUyMoHb","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json, textwrap\np='reference/coverage/mobile-android.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nst=json.load(open('.run/prebuild-state.json'))\nbuilt=sorted(k.split(':',1)[1] for k,v in st.items() if k.startswith('mobile-android:') and (v.get('ok') or v.get('attempts',0)>=2))\na=s.index(\"Priority 1 = plausible within ~3 days.\")\nb=s.index(\"```json\")\nhead='''Priority 1 = plausible within ~3 days. \"prebuild\" = pure-python extractor in `lib/android.py` style that races in\n`solve.py`. \"tool\" = install. \"note\" = doc/prompt change. Already built or given up (prebuild-state ok / attempts>=2, dropped from the list):\n'''\nlst='\\n'.join(textwrap.wrap(', '.join(built)+'.', 118))\nfc='''\nForecast after D25: the MASVS-RESILIENCE arc keeps naming one control per day (D21 anti-debug, D22 root, D23 hook,\nD24 emulator, D25 Play Integrity verdict) and the TT chain absorbs each as one pure gate fn (D25 only changed the gate\nsignature to `(long,int)->long` and dropped to 2 probes). The real escalation moved into Mastery: regenerated OLD days\nnow execute their own mechanic (D25 d19 real reflection, d16 native u16 gate). Mastery picks one old day per 3-day\nstride and +1 set/day (D26 ~10 sets); never-yet-v2 days d05, d08, d11, d12, d13, d18, d20, d21 are due -- d20\n(DexClassLoader payload), d18 (decryptByte strings) and d21 (debugger state loop) are the costly ones. Still unnamed\nfor D26-D31 (6 days left): anti-tamper / repackaging / signature, certificate pinning, key attestation, then obfuscation\ncapstones (flattening, VM, white-box) and probably a final all-days capstone. Mastery solve time doubled D24->D25\n(0.94 -> 1.89 s): keep per-set cost flat as the bundle grows.\n\n'''\ns=s[:a]+head+lst+'\\n'+fc+s[b:]\n# JSON\nj0=s.index(\"```json\")+len(\"```json\"); j1=s.index(\"```\", j0)\ngaps=json.loads(s[j0:j1])\ngaps=[g for g in gaps if g['id'] not in built]\nbyid={g['id']:g for g in gaps}\ndef setp(i,pr,detail_prefix=None):\n    byid[i]['priority']=pr\n    if detail_prefix: byid[i]['detail']=detail_prefix+' '+byid[i]['detail']\nsetp('pinned-emulator-env-profile',2,'D25 note: the emulator theme passed with no env read in any dex; first prebuild attempt failed (ok:false) -- retry once.')\nsetp('mastery-set-scaling-bench',1,'D25: 9 sets took 1.89 s solve (D24 8 sets 0.94 s) -- the per-set cost roughly doubled with the new d19 reflection / d16 gated-native sets; find which set is slow first.')\nsetp('analysis-cert-pin-digest-chain',1)\nsetp('native-bridge-jnienv-callbacks',2,'D25 d16 set added an int arg + u16 gate (`nativeShare(long,int)`) but still no JNIEnv use; first attempt failed (ok:false).')\nsetp('dex-eval-java-random-lcg',2,'First attempt failed (ok:false); d14 regenerated sets use an inline LCG table, not java.util.Random, so far.')\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"v2-dexloader-payload-invoke\",\"concept\":\"v2 chain calls into a second dex: DexClassLoader / InMemoryDexClassLoader over assets/payload.dex + loadClass + getMethod/getDeclaredMethod.invoke (rows 42, 100, 101)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D25 showed regenerated old-day Mastery sets now RUN their mechanic (d19 real reflection). d20 (Loaded Later) has never been a v2 set; its mechanic is a secondary dex. Expect host code: `new DexClassLoader(path, ctx.getCodeCacheDir().getPath(), null, getClassLoader())` after copying `getAssets().open(\\\"payload.dex\\\")` to a file, or `new InMemoryDexClassLoader(ByteBuffer.wrap(bytes), parent)`; then `loadClass(\\\"com.huntress.arena.payload.Module\\\")` -> `getMethod(name, long.class).invoke(null, Long.valueOf(v))` -> unbox. Deep evaluator: model AssetManager.open/InputStream.read/readAllBytes/ByteArrayOutputStream/FileOutputStream as in-memory bytes from the APK entry, parse the payload dex (also xor/b64-wrapped: reuse payload-magic-known-plaintext-unwrap), register its classes in a second class table consulted by loadClass (parent-first: host classes win on name clash, per classloader-shadow-resolve), and continue evaluation inside it (static fields, <clinit>). Test with a synthetic chain built from the D20 payload.dex fixture.\"},\n {\"id\":\"v2-string-decrypt-name-resolve\",\"concept\":\"v2 chain decrypts its own strings (d18 decryptByte) and feeds them to reflection / class lookup / the hex table (rows 35, 43, 70, 100)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"d18 (Encrypted Strings) has never been a v2 set; combined with D25's real reflection, a regenerated d18 set would build method/class names or the `0123456789ABCDEF` table from byte[]/char[] arrays via `decryptByte(b, i)` (`b ^ k ^ i`, `(b - k) & 0xff`, key array cycled) then `new String(bytes, StandardCharsets.UTF_8|US_ASCII|ISO_8859_1)`, `String.valueOf(char[])`, `new String(char[])`, `toCharArray`, `getBytes`, `intern`. Make the deep evaluator exact for: fill-array-data, byte sign extension (`int-to-byte`), char arithmetic (`int-to-char`), String(byte[], charset name or Charset object), StandardCharsets static fields, Charset.forName, String.format, then reflection lookups using the decrypted name. Regression: D18 TT dex helpers + a synthetic chain.\"},\n {\"id\":\"v2-debugger-gate-state-loop\",\"concept\":\"v2 chain with the d21 anti-debug mechanic as code: debuggerGate state machine (while/packed-switch) over Debug/ApplicationInfo/TracerPid/timing probes (rows 41, 79, 88, 100)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"d21 (Debug Me If You Can) has never been a v2 set; its theme words are 'clean-room anti-debug state machine while retaining the intended app flow'. Expect `int state = S0; while (state != DONE) switch (state) { ... }` with transitions on `Debug.isDebuggerConnected()`, `Debug.waitingForDebugger()`, `(ctx.getApplicationInfo().flags & FLAG_DEBUGGABLE) != 0` (D21 manifests set debuggable=true -> read the APK's OWN manifest flag, but the 'intended flow' is the non-debugged path: report both), `/proc/self/status` TracerPid read via BufferedReader(FileReader), `SystemClock.elapsedRealtime()` deltas. Evaluator: clean answers (false / TracerPid:\\\\t0 / small monotonic delta), a loop-iteration cap, and for ApplicationInfo.flags evaluate both manifest-true and clean-false, preferring the value that keeps the chain on its non-trap path (no -1/0 sentinel). Reuse anti-debug-state-machine-clean-path + flattened-cfg-switch-eval helpers inside _DxeDeepVM.\"},\n {\"id\":\"v2-app-state-first-run-defaults\",\"concept\":\"v2 chain reading app-private state (SharedPreferences, SQLite, Keystore, backup flags) answered as a fresh install (rows 16-18, 31, 100)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"d05 (backup), d11 (SharedPreferences), d12 (SQLite) and d13 (Keystore) are due as v2 Mastery sets with their mechanic in code. Intrinsics for the deep evaluator: `ctx.getSharedPreferences(name, mode)` -> empty store whose getLong/getInt/getString/getBoolean return the DEFAULT arg, edit().putX().apply()/commit() then readable in the same run; `SQLiteOpenHelper`/`openOrCreateDatabase` + execSQL CREATE/INSERT + rawQuery/Cursor.moveToFirst/getLong/getString over a tiny in-memory sqlite3 (python stdlib) -- statements are dex const-strings; `KeyStore.getInstance(\\\"AndroidKeyStore\\\").load(null)`, containsAlias -> false on first run, `size()` 0; `ApplicationInfo.flags` FLAG_ALLOW_BACKUP (0x8000) / FLAG_USES_CLEARTEXT_TRAFFIC (0x8000000) / FLAG_DEBUGGABLE (2) from the APK's own manifest; `NetworkSecurityPolicy.getInstance().isCleartextTrafficPermitted(host)` from the NSC xml. Abort a candidate (not invent) on unmodelled state.\"},\n {\"id\":\"v2-reflection-api-breadth\",\"concept\":\"reflection variants beyond D25's forName+getDeclaredMethod+invoke inside the v2 evaluator (rows 43, 77, 80)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D25 d19 set: `\\\"m\\\"+dispatch(k)` -> Class.forName -> getDeclaredMethod(name, Long.TYPE) -> invoke(null, Long) -> check-cast Long -> longValue. Next generator steps: iterate `getDeclaredMethods()`/`getMethods()` filtering on getName().equals/hashCode()/startsWith or on an annotation, `Method.getParameterTypes().length`, `getDeclaredField(name).getLong(null)` / `Field.setAccessible(true)`, `getDeclaredConstructor().newInstance()` + instance invoke, `Class.getName()/getSimpleName()` used as hash input, `MethodHandles.lookup().findStatic(cls, name, MethodType.methodType(long.class, long.class)).invokeExact(v)`, `Integer.TYPE` vs `Integer.class` boxing, InvocationTargetException wrapping. Define dex method/field ORDER as declared-order (dex class_data order) and document it; sort-sensitive generators may rely on it.\"}\n]\ngaps.extend(new)\norder={'note':1,'prebuild':0,'tool':2}\ngaps.sort(key=lambda g:(g['priority'], order[g['action']]))\ns=s[:j0]+'[\\n'+',\\n'.join('  '+json.dumps(g, ensure_ascii=False) for g in gaps)+'\\n]\\n'+s[j1:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\npend=[g['id'] for g in gaps if g['action']=='prebuild' and g['id'] not in built]\nprint(len(pend), pend)\nEOF","description":"Rewrite readiness gaps, forecast and JSON queue"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1073,"cache_read_input_tokens":121921,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1073},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"42f33c12-3125-441c-8886-1e987da4999d","uuid":"20d4170d-56bb-4862-bcbc-b82653a005f6","timestamp":"2026-10-25T13:13:03.196Z","request_id":"req_011CgP1inm9kaL3xazf7drrz","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Np14p3whLXDS